            "text": "{\n  \"verdict\": \"ACCEPTED\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"missing_assumptions\": [],\n  \"counterexamples\": [],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"The theorem strictly requires the carrier class to include arbitrarily large finite fans (unbounded branching); the empty-leaf condition (E0) cannot be derived from positivity and the ledger on any fixed finite universe or bounded-branching class.\",\n    \"The result applies to formal mathematical holdings (the ownership model), which does not automatically identify these holdings with physically accessible records, arbitrary detector outputs, or normalized event probabilities.\",\n    \"Positivity (POS) is a required premise on the formal holdings themselves; it is not an automatic consequence of the positivity of native input grades.\",\n    \"The occurrence of the P1 event, the physical event typing, and the preparability of the initial states remain assumed empirical inputs.\"\n  ],\n  \"constructive_analysis\": [\n    \"The arbitrary finite fan argument $n A(d,m) \\\\le \\\\kappa$ is mathematically sound and elegantly forces every off-diagonal $\\\\nu$ entry to vanish over $\\\\mathbb{Q}$ or $\\\\mathbb{R}$. By attaching $n$ leaves to a depth $d-1$ vertex and placing a unit grade at depth $m \u003c d$, the source cone totals dictate that each leaf holds $A(d,m)$. Positivity ensures $A(d,m) \\\\ge 0$, and conservation bounds the sum $n A(d,m)$ by the total holding $\\\\kappa$. Since $n$ can be arbitrarily large, $A(d,m)$ must be exactly zero, proving $\\\\nu$ is diagonal.\",\n    \"The iff classification by a nonnegative nonincreasing depth sequence $a_k$ is rigorously proved. The diagonal $\\\\nu$ yields $H_v = a_k c_v - a_{k+1} \\\\sum c_u$. Testing with a unit at a leaf gives $a_k \\\\ge 0$, and testing with a unit at a child gives $a_k - a_{k+1} \\\\ge 0$, perfectly recovering the monotonicity and sign conditions.\",\n    \"Zero-extension naturality (W2) is successfully derived without being assumed. Because new vertices under zero extension have zero source cones and old source cones are unchanged, the diagonal holding formula $s_v = a_{k_v} c_v$ naturally assigns zero holding to new vertices and preserves old holdings.\",\n    \"The deduction that (W1) and (W4) imply (PN) and (W2) is correct. Conservation of total holding (W1) combined with the unchanged holdings of non-receivers (W4) algebraically forces the receiver to absorb exactly the pruned leaf's holding, which is exactly (PN). Theorem 1 then supplies (W2).\",\n    \"The local acquisition criterion is accurately verified. The pre-event contrast $g(a_{d-1} - a_d)$ and post-event contrast $g a_{d-1}$ correctly show that the receiver's holding is initially identical and becomes separated exactly when $a_{d-1} = a_d \u003e 0$. This proves that local acquisition does not require a universal climb or full global coordinate identification.\",\n    \"The bounded-root-degree $\\\\epsilon$ counterfamily is a rigorous and highly valuable control. It proves that without unbounded fan sizes, a compensated empty-branch assignment can satisfy (PN), (POS), and conservation while violating (E0). The specialization to $B = N-1$ correctly demonstrates that the theorem fails on any entire finite universe of size $N$.\",\n    \"The explicit boundaries are honest and sufficient. The manuscript clearly distinguishes formal ownership from actual accessible records, explicitly states that positivity of inputs does not imply positivity of holdings, and acknowledges that event typing and preparability remain open.\"\n  ],\n  \"native_bridge_status\": \"NOT_DERIVED\",\n  \"next_native_obligation\": \"Identify a source-backed receiver record whose nonnegative holdings obey the pruning ledger and whose carrier-composition domain supports the needed fan comparisons (or establish its empty-leaf property directly on the actual domain). Then check the existing record on one preparable blind-to-distinguished event, without defining t